load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A basis of a vector space: a minimal set of vectors from which every vector is a unique combination, the coordinate
# axes once chosen. Its size is the dimension. The twenty-four directions of the 24-cell are not a basis (they
# overdetermine the four-dimensional space) but a root system, a more symmetric spanning set. The form carries the
# vector space; spanning and independence are the basis conditions.
form basis
  link space, like vector-space
